   "html_text": "Scientific behaviorism faced similar challenges. The theories of Watson, Skinner, et al had some early successes, especially in the domain of animal learning, and its principles are still used, at least for heuristic purposes, in various areas of psychology. But as many psychologists (and others, e.g. Chomsky 1959) have argued, the successes of behaviorism seem to depend upon the experimenters’ implicit control of certain variables which, when made explicit, involve ineliminable reference to org",
